{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1207420-homebrew-path-inspired-by-the-secret-world-mellificus-the-animancer","id":1207420,"title":"[Homebrew path inspired by The secret world] - Mellificus: The Animancer","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-15T15:20:54-07:00","id":1207420,"title":"[Homebrew path inspired by The secret world] - Mellificus: The Animancer","content":"<i>Magic is a bond. you're Hanging over the void but kept safe by your ties to it while you try and reach for the Stars<br /> <br /> We awoke to the seret sounds of the world, the sweet buzzing that connect and the titanic powers that keep the sacred equilibrium<br /> we don the amber crown and welcomes inside of us the forces and patterns that shape and move the universe, we are the protectors.<br /> <br /> We walked the ever reaching path of Agartha, the world inside of us all and followed the signal to it's source, we reached the tower of the Amber crown and by imprinting our names on its walls, we accept our duty. Magic is not far, it's everywhere, the fallen world still longs for the supernal, we know the sweet melodies that will move the inanimate, the secret power that course inside our veins, the ever moving force that bind us all. But there is a dissonance in our sweet cacophony, an horrible song that deafen the honeyed creaks of the cogs, the endless screams of those who were never meant to be, the abyss is here, it is ever expanding, will you sit still while it consume everything in its nightmarish fever dream ? Or will you stand up an call the might of the world around you ? I know you're scared,but if we do not make a stand right here, right now, there may never be another chance for us, keep hope, what as fallen may rise again.<br /> <br /> What has fallen may yet rise again.</i><br /> <br /> She's an <b>Animancer</b>, a crafter, she takes bits of matter, mix them together and whispers a sweet song so it will rise and follow her every commands. She can change everything around her, if she need something, she simply put her hands to the earth and extract all the material as mother earth recognize her divine powers.<br /> He's a <b>Magister</b>, he hear te vibrations of the atoms, and split them with a sound, all of the natural world respond to his cry for help, he is infused with the raw might of the world, Lighting lend him his might, fire cower before him and gravity helps him in his endeavor <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Mellificus magic<br /> <br /> Ruling Arcana</b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Force and Matter</b>, they are the building block of the fallen world, matter is everywhere, connected by a constant ebb and flow of differents forces in a sublime balance that the Mellificus instinctively know. The body might be alive, but it is purely living matter that interact with itself by means of electricity.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Inferior Arcana</b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Prime :</b> Every Animancer knows of the supernal realms, But surely Agartha is within us ? The wolrd is teeming with power already ! Mellificus have a difficult time understanding that the Fallen world is but a Shadow of supernal thruth, some Mage theorizes that this impedement hinder the Mellificus understanding of the Mysteries and their progression or worse, make them more suseptible to becoming Banisher, a theory you better not tell the Magisters, for their temper is short and their wrath match even the mighty Obrimos.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Symbolism </b></span><br /> The Mellificus are the <b>Hanged man</b> They embrace their new perspective on the world, seeing its natural components interracting and must choose how they will use their power, at the same time the <b>Star </b>gives them the inspiration to transcend themselves and to protect the world<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Supernal realm : Agartha </span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The hollow earth, the neural path of the world itself, Agartha is an endless crossroads of tree branches steaming with electricity and arcane machinery, The Supernal habitants of this realm are collectively called the <b>Guardians </b> and are divised into <b>Titans</b>, the recondites beings of matter, Huge impossible arcanic automatons running on sweet honey, they are eternal and ever patient, but their power is </span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">incommensurable</span><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">. the <b>Drones</b> are the recondites beings of forces they transport the life blood of Argatha, taking the forms of sprites of differents forces, they are flilimsy, ever moving and always cheerfull, but do not take their joyous demeanor for friendliness, they are power made manifest and their taunting and riddles may be deadly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>New merit : Hacked signal \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <i>*BUZZING STATIC* WHAT HAS FALLEN MAY RISE AGAIN WHAT HAS *SCREECING SOUND* </i><br /> Something went very wrong with your awakening, you see cogs and hears the turning of gears everywhere, you gain Prime as another ruling arcanum but can never join any legacies, your souls has been shaped by an </span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">unknown</span> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> entity and you feel compell to follow its agenda, every chapter your Storyteller may imposed the Urged condition on you, you may not gain any beat by resolving this special condition.</span></span></span></span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T17:05:58-07:00","id":1207455,"title":"","content":"Not knowing the source inspiration material but knowing some Mage 1E books, any chance these guys are related to the \u201ctrue Material Realm\u201d mentioned in Summoners?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T19:11:04-07:00","id":1207478,"title":"","content":"Hum i haven't summoner in a while so i'll have to check on that, But the thing is that Agartha is the concept of a realm inside the earth, i'll read Sumonners again to see if i can make any kind of connection ( as for the source material <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YPxDsaR9RBE\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YPxDsaR9RBE</a>, i thought of giving the Mellificus Life and space as ruling arcana at some point)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T02:20:06-07:00","id":1207588,"title":"","content":"I noticed that both ruling Arcana are gross rather than one gross and one subtle like the five original Paths. Is this deliberate?<br /> <br /> Hacked Signal, why not allow the subject to gain Beats that way?<br /> <br /> With that Merit I get some God-Machine vibes. As if it's a Rank ~8 Supernal Entity from the realm of Agartha that wasn't just outright destroyed by the Abyss, but rather warped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T12:20:24-07:00","id":1207726,"title":"","content":"Unless &quot;What has fallen may rise again&quot; are the arc words of the Secret World game too, then I think that was deliberate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T12:55:19-07:00","id":1207733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1207420-homebrew-path-inspired-by-the-secret-world-mellificus-the-animancer?p=1207588#post1207588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I noticed that both ruling Arcana are gross rather than one gross and one subtle like the five original Paths. Is this deliberate?<br /> <br /> Hacked Signal, why not allow the subject to gain Beats that way?<br /> <br /> With that Merit I get some God-Machine vibes. As if it's a Rank ~8 Supernal Entity from the realm of Agartha that wasn't just outright destroyed by the Abyss, but rather warped.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yep the two Gross arcanum were a deliberate choice, as for the Hacked signal, i tought being able to begin playing with three ruling arcanum was pretty powerfull boon in itself and needed to be balanced.<br /> <br /> The theme of a machine deity is present in the secret world, so i linked it to the God machine instead, as the Mellificus are tied to gross &quot;fallen&quot; arcanum the Machine grant them a bit of supernal light with the Prime arcanum","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}